	<section_number>2.2-500</section_number>
	<catch_line>Attorney General to be chief executive officer; duties generally</catch_line>
	<text>
		The Attorney General shall be the chief executive officer of the Department of Law, and shall perform such duties as may be provided by law.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1950, § 2-85; 1966, c. 677, § 2.1-117; 2001, c. 844.</history>
